I went to the Flickr Creative Commons section:

http://www.flickr.com/creativecommons/by-nc-sa-2.0/

Creative Commons makes it all work really well!  There's plenty of  
good free pictures to use, and then once we've made collections of  
them we already know it's allowed to reassemble & rearrange & reuse  
them again, so from there we can put together paper books or include  
them in teaching materials or whatever.

Whenever anyone labels a single picture with a single caption, it'll  
be useful, because over time we can gather everyone's work together  
and put it all in a context that makes it accessible for learners.

